INSTALL — cugpt build instructions

DEPENDENCIES
============

  microgpt.c requires only:
    - A C compiler (gcc or clang)
    - libm (standard math library, always present)

  cugpt.c additionally requires:
    - libopenblas-dev  (Ubuntu/Debian: apt install libopenblas-dev)
    - cblas.h header   (included with libopenblas-dev)

  microgpt.py requires:
    - Python 3.6+  (no third-party packages)

  The benchmark target (make bench) also requires:
    - python3 in PATH

QUICK BUILD
===========

  make            # builds both microgpt and cugpt
  ./microgpt      # train + infer (downloads input.txt if needed)
  ./cugpt         # train + infer (downloads input.txt if needed)

MANUAL BUILD
============

  # microgpt (no external deps):
  cc -O3 -march=native -ffast-math -o microgpt microgpt.c -lm

  # cugpt (requires OpenBLAS):
  cc -O3 -march=native -ffast-math -o cugpt cugpt.c -lopenblas -lm

  # If cblas.h is not on the default include path:
  cc -O3 -march=native -ffast-math \
     -I/usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu \
     -o cugpt cugpt.c -lopenblas -lm

INSTALL / UNINSTALL
===================

  make install    # copies binaries to $(PREFIX)/bin  [default: /usr/local]
  make uninstall

  To install to a custom prefix:
    make install PREFIX=$HOME/.local

PYTHON REFERENCE
================

  python3 microgpt.py

  No pip packages required. Downloads input.txt automatically on first run.
